Answer background wifi secret requests with the saved key.

After a failed 4-way handshake NetworkManager discards the stored PSK and asks
the secret agents for a new one, also when it reconnects on its own, e.g. after
the AP switches channels. The agent's prompt only lives in the control center's
network tab, so nobody sees it: NM times out after 120 s, fails the activation
with no-secrets, and blocks the profile from autoconnecting until the user
reconnects by hand. For requests the user didn't initiate, hand back the key NM
sent along, so NM just retries; user-initiated connects still prompt.

--- a/src/dbus/network/network_secret_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/dbus/network/network_secret_agent.cpp
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
   constexpr auto kAgentManagerInterface = "org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.AgentManager";
 
   constexpr std::uint32_t kNmSecretAgentGetSecretsFlagAllowInteraction = 0x1;
+  constexpr std::uint32_t kNmSecretAgentGetSecretsFlagUserRequested = 0x4;
 
   constexpr auto kWirelessSettingName = "802-11-wireless";
   constexpr auto kWirelessSecuritySettingName = "802-11-wireless-security";
@@ -54,6 +55,23 @@
     }
   }
 
+  // NM only includes system-owned secrets for agents with the modify permission
+  std::string extractPsk(const SecretsDict& connection) {
+    auto wsecIt = connection.find(kWirelessSecuritySettingName);
+    if (wsecIt == connection.end()) {
+      return {};
+    }
+    auto pskIt = wsecIt->second.find(kPskKey);
+    if (pskIt == wsecIt->second.end()) {
+      return {};
+    }
+    try {
+      return pskIt->second.get<std::string>();
+    } catch (const sdbus::Error&) {
+      return {};
+    }
+  }
+
 } // namespace
 
